{% block brandDescription %}
      <p class="brand-description">Founded in 1883 by Friedrich Gretsch in Brooklyn, New York, the Gretsch Company is an iconic American manufacturer renowned for high-quality musical instruments, particularly hollow-body electric guitars that defined the "Great Gretsch Sound" of the 1950s rockabilly and country eras. Now owned by Fender Musical Instruments Corporation, Gretsch remains a premier brand favored by artists like Chet Atkins and George Harrison.<br><a href="#" class="decoder-howto-link" data-modal-target="howto-gretsch">(How to decode a Gretsch serial #)</a></p>
